The best rainbows are the ones you find when you are not looking for them.

One Tuesday, after a long, grey rain, I was walking home from school. My wellies were muddy and my socks were wet. I was thinking about nothing at all.

Then the sun came out. Just a little bit.

I looked up. There, over the park, was a rainbow. It was not a big, grand one. It was small and faint, like a secret. It had two ends, one over the swings and one over the old oak tree.

I stopped. A lady walking her dog stopped too. We did not say a word. We just looked.

That is the kind of rainbow I like best. Not the ones in books, but the quiet ones that appear for a moment, just for you, and then melt away. [end of text]


